{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Architectural Designs"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you talk about programming apps"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "\"Interpret the technical design report, to determine the work plan during the phase of building the software, based on regulation ad protocols established by the company.  Design the architecture design using the appropriate tools and types according to the software requirements. \""}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on persisting storage, web applications, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research about the different types of software architectural designs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select three types of architectural designs and make a brochure comparing and describing them. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare five questions about the software designs for your classmates. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your brochure with your classmates and exchange the questions. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about the different type of software architectural designs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a brochure about the software architectural designs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask to my classmates about software designs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice my pronunciation with my classmates "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Ought to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can express ideas that show advisability by using \u201c<strong>ought to.</strong>\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&ldquo;<b>Ought to</b>&rdquo; is a modal verb; as a modal verb, it follows the next rules:</p> <ul style=\"text-align: justify;\"> <li>&nbsp;Modal verbs always come after the subject and before the main verb.</li> <li>The main verb is always in infinitive form, regardless of the subject (I, you, he, we, etc.).</li> <li>A modal verb should never follow another modal verb in a sentence.</li> </ul> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In terms of meaning, &ldquo;<b>ought to</b>&rdquo; is considered to have the same meaning as &ldquo;should&rdquo; and similar to &ldquo;had better&rdquo; when it is used for giving advice.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;In order to make a sentence with ought to, you can use the following structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b>Subject + ought to + infinitive verb + complement.</b></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Example:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>You <b>ought to</b> identify what the needs of your software are.</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;Notice that the use of &ldquo;ought to&rdquo; in interrogative form is not common, therefore people rather use should instead of ought to when asking questions.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i><b>Ought</b> you&nbsp;<b>to</b> choose a better software architecture</i><i>? (wrong)</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i><b>Should</b> you choose a better software architecture? (right)</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to make use of the first one to receive and send messages by means of more than one communication channel."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to choose between one of the most used ones, that is, the client/server method and the 3-tier one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Similarly, the layered and object oriented architectures ought to be analyzed, as they outline the best way to manage the software."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Common Architectural Designs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Architectural designs provide the software with the framework and patterns to work with. They provide rules for combining and configuring the different components as well as the ways to communicate with each other.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Depending on their area of focus, architectural designs can be organized into 4 basic categories: communication, deployment, domain and structure.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Compare:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Category\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Architectural Design\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"> Brief description</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Communication</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Message bus </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Indicates the use of software that sends and receives messages using more than one channel. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"> Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA)</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Allows the program to send and receive several messages or services to a server through different terminals.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Deployment</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Client/server  </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is a direct connection between the client and the server.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">N-tier (3 tier) </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Divides the tiers into three, where the client does not communicate directly to the server, but to a sub server to process more information.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Domain</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Domain Driven Design </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Implements the business model to link the components in the program.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Component based </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It decomposes the components of the software to individual components.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Structure</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Layered </p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It layers the functions of the components so that a layer can be modified without affecting the others; it is only linked to the previous layer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong></strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"> Object oriented</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It divides the components into independent and reusable objects.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lexicon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "specific or technical vocabulary"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is in charge of providing a combination of lexicon of components and connectors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "glitch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "problem or complication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is in charge of providing a combination of lexicon of components and connectors as well as solutions to possible glitches or complications."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "split "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to separate into two or more parts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Either way, you must analyze the best option for your company, as the client/server architecture will split the communication into two."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "station "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a computer or a server located in an isolated place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: On the other hand, the 3-tier one will divide the deployment of communication into three segments, all in different stations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type":