st as a house, a program needs to be planned and designed before being built so that it doesn&rsquo;t collapse. Such a process is what we identify as software architecture. It is in charge of providing a combination of the lexicon of components and connectors as well as solutions to possible glitches or complications, guaranteeing this way the best functioning of the system. Now, depending on the purpose of your software you might want to analyze the different architectural styles that are there.&nbsp;</p>"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Depending on their category, the architectural designs might change. For example, there are 4 main categories: communication, deployment, domain, and structure. Within the first category, we can find two of the most common architectural styles, the message bus and the service-oriented architecture (SOA). You ought to make use of the first one to receive and send messages by means of more than one communication channel. Similarly, you might want to exploit SOA to define the communication methods, in terms of software that you might want to use in your company.<br />Once you&rsquo;ve decided what communication method to use, you&rsquo;d better choose one deployment method as well, to do so, you ought to choose between one of the most used ones, that is, the client/server method and the 3-tier one. Either way, you must analyze the best option for your company, as the client/server architecture will split the communication into two, allowing the server to communicate directly with the client and vice versa. On the other hand, the 3-tier one will divide the deployment of communication into three segments, all in different stations.&nbsp;</p>"}, {"time": "103000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Finally, you might want to choose the best architecture regarding the domain and the structure of your software. The domain driven design and the component-based architectures are two of the best architectures you might want to implement, as they both focus on communication channels within the domain. Similarly, the layered and object-oriented architectures ought to be analyzed, as they outline the best way to manage the software, in terms of structure; here you&rsquo;d better select the one that best divides the software, that is, layers or objects that contain the data and behavior of your system.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le01ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}